int[][] t = {{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5}, {6}};
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < t.length; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < t[0].length; j++) {
        sum += t[i][j];
    }
}
System.out.println(sum);

Question: What is printed? Explain how the inner loop decides how many columns to visit.

